	   ***  tao v3.3 PARAMETERS FILE  ***
	       (default unities : I.S.)

PARAMETER	CORRESPONDING 		USE
 VALUES		  VARIABLES
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Gridding:
401		nx		Number of x points (distance).
101		nz		Number of z points (depth for rheological calculations).

Limits:
0e3		x0		Modelizated x range.
500e3		xf

Window:
0e3		xmin		Limits of the output window.
300e3		xmax
-10000		ymin
-4000		ymax


Lithosph. geometry:
17000		espelastdefault	Default ET (if no .EET file) 
32000		espcortdefault	Default crustal geometry for gravity anomaly
15000		espcortsup 	  and rheological calculations when no .CRUST and .UCRUST
0  -5800		alt0 		Altitude of  the initial plate position from sea level.


Densities:
3300		densmanto	Mantle.
2900		denscort	Crust (just for anomaly calculation).
2800		densinfill	Infilling material (only when switch_topoest=1).
2300		denssedim	Sediments.
1013		densamb		Air (or water for oceanic flexure).


Erosion model parameters (used only if switch_erosed=1):
0e6		Kerosdif, 	Diffusive erosion constant [m2/Ma].
0e-15		Keroseol, 	Continental background erosion rate constant meters of sediment by meters of height and My [m/(m·Ma)].
.0		Ksedim, 	Water sedimentation rate [m/Ma].



Time variables [Ma]:
0		Timeini		Initial time.
1		Timefinal	Final time.
5		tau		Relaxation time (used only if switch_viscoelast=1).
2		dt		Increment time.
10		dtmemounit	Time elapsed between units recording. 
				  if = 0 only file-defined load units will be recorded. 


Boundary Conditions:
1		boundary_conds	#0: Continuous simetric half-plate.
				#1: Broken plate (left).
				#2: Continuous plate.
				#3: Free ends.
				#4: Hunging plate.
				#5: Broken plate (right).

External forces:
0e12	tecforce	Horizontal tectonic force (compressive if >0).
0e12	appshearforce	Applied force as bound. cond. in case 1. (left side) (downwards if <0).
0e17	appmoment 	Torque as bound. cond. case 1. (left side) (clockwise if >0).


2	lith_type		To switch rheological calculations:
				#-1: No flexure performance.
				#0: Pure elastic plate model.
				#1: Visco-elastic plate model.
				#2: Elastic-plastic oceanic lithosphere.
				#3: Elastic-plastic continental always decoupled.
				#4: Elastic-plastic continental never decoupled.
				#5: Elastic-plastic continental auto. decoupling.


These are switches to turn on options of the model.
Their possible values are 1 (yes) or 0 (no):
0	switch_sea		For existence of sea.
0	switch_erosed		For erosional-deositional model.
0	grav_anom_type		Gravity anomaly output type. #0: No gravity calculations; #1: Bouguer anomaly;  #2:Free-Air

i/o switches:
1	switch_write_file	For file output.
0	switch_ps		For postscript output.
0	switch_output		For graphic output(PV-WAVE).
0	switch_verbose		For more runtime prints.
0	switch_debug		For more runtime prints.
